    "concept": {
      "variant_id": "B2-v002",
      "brief_id": "B2",
      "direction": "soft_pebble",
      "name": "Pebble Grip AQD",
      "form_language": "Soft pebble slab with fully continuous convex surfaces; no sharp transitions anywhere. Plan-view sides bow outward with a subtle waist, vertical edges roll into generous 12 mm radii, and the top/bottom faces crown gently giving a pillow-like cross-section. A continuous raised bumper band wraps the entire perimeter at the mid-height parting line, swelling 2.5 mm proud of the shell and acting as the sacrificial drop feature plus grip rail. The front face is a single recessed instrument panel: a dark tinted polycarbonate display window sits high, framed by a shallow 0.8 mm shadow groove, while below it a high-visibility orange shell face carries a deep grille of horizontal intake slots with 1.2 mm ribs, sunk 1.5 mm into the crown so slot lips are protected from abrasion. Two glove-scale concave thumb scallops are moulded into the left and right flanks. All corners are enlarged radius lobes that overhang the internal chassis, giving the internals a suspended, shock-isolated mount. Overall it reads as a friendly river stone that happens to be safety orange.",
      "silhouette": "pebble",
