      "cmf": {
        "material": "PC-ABS",
        "finish": "textured_heavy",
        "color": "Safety orange shell (UV-stabilised), charcoal grey display bezel and bumper accent, matte non-reflective",
        "secondary_ops": [
          "soft_touch",
          "pad_print",
          "laser_etch"
        ]
      },
      "intent_anchors": [
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA1",
          "statement": "Keep the continuous 12 mm perimeter bumper band 2.5 mm proud of the shell on all four sides and both end lobes; it is the primary 1.5 m drop-energy absorber and must not be flattened, interrupted by openings, or reduced below 2.0 mm proud for cosmetic reasons.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA2",
          "statement": "Preserve the pebble silhouette with continuous convex curvature and no flats or sharp edges: minimum external radius 10 mm on all vertical and horizontal transitions so the device cannot present a hard strike edge to concrete.",
          "category": "form",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA3",
          "statement": "Preserve the recessed intake grille geometry: horizontal slots with >=15% open area, slot lips sunk at least 1.5 mm below the surrounding shell crown, backed by a serviceable ePTFE membrane and perimeter gasket to hold IP65.",
          "category": "usability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA4",
          "statement": "Preserve the glove-scale side thumb scallops (min 18 mm wide, 6 mm deep concavity per flank) and the heavy moulded texture (Ra >= 3.2 um equivalent) on shell and bumper; these are the wet/muddy glove grip features and must not be smoothed to improve appearance.",
          "category": "usability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA5",
          "statement": "Keep the display window a separate dark-tinted PC lens with a 0.8 mm shadow groove and a compressed gasket seal; do not merge it into a single clear-over-moulded shell, as the gasketed lens is the IP65 front-face seal strategy.",
          "category": "durability",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA6",
          "statement": "Hold the shell in UV-stabilised PC-ABS with textured_heavy mould finish and safety orange pigment rated for >=3 years outdoor colour and impact retention; do not substitute unstabilised ABS or a glossy finish to cut cost.",
          "category": "cmf",
          "must_preserve": true
        },
        {
          "anchor_id": "IA7",
          "statement": "Maintain the internal shock-isolation scheme: the moulded corner lobes must overhang the internal chassis so the ~92 g internals are suspended on ribbed elastomeric mounts, keeping the housing at <=180 g total with single-shot mouldings and no added metal brackets.",
          "category": "cost",
          "must_preserve": true
        }
      ],
      "rationale": "The soft_pebble direction is chosen because a fully convex, bumpers-in-the-round form is the cheapest way to pass a 1.5 m six-face concrete drop: energy is dissipated by continuous curvature and a sacrificial proud band rather than by extra wall thickness, keeping the PC-ABS shot weight inside the CNY 18 ceiling at 10k units/year. The perimeter bumper is moulded integrally in the same tool (one extra slider, no second material), so it delivers protected corners without a TPE overmould line; a small soft_touch patch is reserved only for the two thumb scallops where grip is critical. PC-ABS is selected over ABS for notched impact at low temperature and over rABS for UV/colour confidence, with heavy texture hiding scuffs and providing wet-glove friction. The front-face stack is deliberate: dark tinted display high (readable while held, protected by the crown above it), recessed intake slots low and sunk below the crown so they cannot be abraded or puddle-filled, and the USB port moved to the bottom face where a captive gasketed flap is easiest to seal and least likely to be knocked open in use. All openings and the parting line sit in the shadow of the bumper band, which simplifies gasket routing and keeps IP65 achievable with a single perimeter seal plus lens and port gaskets, consistent with the rule-based ePTFE vent resolution. Intent anchors lock the drop-critical bumper, the no-sharp-edge silhouette, the sealed lens and grille architecture, the glove-grip texture, the UV-stabilised PC-ABS spec, and the weight/cost-preserving internal suspension, so downstream engineering cannot trade away ruggedness for styling."
    },
